// RegControl idle-zone suppression, EPRI r4133 semantics (BUG WP
// regcontrol_idle, 2026-07-19). `idle=yes` on a reversible regulator makes
// `Sample` read the through-power and, when it lands in the BOUNDED no-load
// band [RevPowerThreshold, FwdPowerThreshold] (default −100/+100 kW), drop the
// pending tap change ("idle in no-load zone"). r4133 RegControl.pas:1218 tests
// this with an `and` — idle only when the through-power is SMALL. (dss_capi
// 0.15.x wrote the same test as an `or`, a tautology under the symmetric band
// that made an idling reg never tap; the port previously reproduced that and
// diverged 8.8% from r4133. The WP adopted r4133's `and`; see STATUS
// "BUG WP regcontrol_idle".)
//
// Feature sensitivity: the load pulls the regulated bus far below the 128 V
// target, so the through-power is LARGE (well outside ±100 kW). It therefore
// falls OUTSIDE the no-load band, idle does NOT suppress, and the regulator
// taps all the way up — tapnum 15, tap 1.09375, MV.1 ≈ 7650.08 V, |V| ≈ 0.939
// pu, identical to idle=no. `idle` is a 0.15.x/r4133-only property (0.14.5
// rejects it with #110), so this deck gates on the r4133 channel only. The
// revThreshold/fwdThreshold getter-convention residual is pinned as an
// exact-pair ledger divergence (r4133-regcontrol-idle-threshold-display); the
// tap/voltage physics gate live.
//
// Gating oracle: EPRI r4133 (engines: r4133) via epri-worker.
clear
Set DefaultBaseFrequency=60

New circuit.regidle basekv=12.47 pu=1.0 phases=3 bus1=src
~ mvasc3=20000 mvasc1=21000

New transformer.tr phases=3 windings=2 buses=(src, mv) conns=(wye wye)
~ kvs=(12.47 12.47) kvas=(10000 10000) xhl=7

New line.l1 phases=3 bus1=mv bus2=ld r1=0.4 x1=0.7 c1=0 length=4 units=km

New load.ld bus1=ld phases=3 conn=wye model=1 kv=12.47 kw=7000 pf=0.95

// Reversible regulator with idle=yes: the deep under-voltage drives a large
// through-power (outside the ±100 kW no-load band), so idle does NOT suppress
// and the regulator taps up (r4133 bounded-AND semantics).
New regcontrol.rg transformer=tr winding=2 vreg=128 band=1 ptratio=60
~ reversible=yes idle=yes

Set voltagebases=[12.47]
calcv
Set mode=snap
Set controlmode=static
Solve
